radoxically considered by many to be the best of Swans' career, despite coming out of a period of immense creative, audience, and musical focus crisis. Michael Gira, believing Swans was \"dead,\" compiled and reworked a multitude of ideas accumulated over the previous 12-13 years of the band's existence. The album masterfully collects all of Swans' diverse stages: from their early hard noise rock to the softer, more melodic period with Jarboe, and even the more banal melodic rock that followed the \"Love Will Tear Us Apart\" cover. It functions as a \"farewell compilation,\" packaging the best of these often disjointed stages into a surprisingly cohesive and brilliant work. It received fantastic reviews in both Europe and the United States, leading many publications like Pitchfork and AllMusic to re-evaluate and update their initially horrible reviews of Swans' early albums. \"En el 96 sale el que para muchos es el mejor disco de su carrera, curiosamente después de todo ese problema creativo.\"","year":1996,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"SWANS. Una visión del rock diferente","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sJ3HuN7woDc"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":195559733093722,"artist":"Swans","artist_id":188548856103507,"title":"Soundtracks For The Blind","year":1996,"ess":0,"yt":"2NOc1Gnu18I","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Minimal-rock: Sonic Youth y Swans","scene_id":179922132646505,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#minimal-rock","chapters":["Sección 5.13"],"pages":[[1,168,null]]}],"others":[{"id":27832509207602,"type":"album","name":"Filth","year":1983,"weight":51},{"id":67554303296747,"type":"album","name":"To Be Kind","year":2014,"weight":41},{"id":179224173187400,"type":"album","name":"Swans Are Dead","year":1998,"weight":32},{"id":177036821134110,"type":"album","name":"White Light From The Mouth Of Infi